executionContract.intendedBehavior:
moe.chat_wait's backlog drains (entry and wake) apply the live wake's relevance rule. Outside the caller's channels filter, or in every scanned channel when there is no filter, they deliver only lines routed to the caller:
- a mention that MentionRouter.parseMentions resolves to the caller, directly or through a group;
- a line that names no seat and was sent by 'system' or 'human';
- with no filter, any 'human' line.
Watched channels keep returning everything. Lines the drain reads and skips advance that channel's cursor, and they clear its unread when the channel was read to its end, so no later call delivers them. A filtered channel reads past up to 10 full pages of skipped lines per drain, so a routed line further down is still delivered in the same call. An entry drain that only skipped lines writes that bookkeeping before it blocks.
